# Chart Widget

The `chart` widget renders ECharts-based visualizations with optional presets for common patterns.

## Design-system conventions

- Use canonical chart palettes: `default`, `ocean`, `sunset`.
- Prefer named design-system colors or palette colors before introducing raw hex values.
- Treat semantic status colors (`success`, `warning`, `destructive`, etc.) as meaning-bearing accents, not a substitute for a full chart palette.
- If MCP resources are available, inspect `skipper://design-system` and `skipper://design-system/palettes` first.

## Basic structure

```yaml
- id: my_chart
  type: chart
  col_span: 12
  datasource: web5_costs               # Key from datasources or projection
  # OR inline SQL (auto-creates a type: view datasource as {widget.id}__view):
  # datasource:
  #   sql: |
  #     SELECT date, SUM(costs) as costs FROM {{source:web5_costs}} GROUP BY date
  title: "Web5 Costs"                   # Optional. Widget header title
  chart_title: "Revenue trend"          # Optional. ECharts canvas title (inside chart area)
  preset: trend                         # Optional. Preset layout
  chart_type: bar                       # Optional. Override chart type
  sort: value_desc                      # Optional. Sort order for X-axis categories
  drill_down: true                      # Optional. Enable drill-down (boolean or object)
  # Or explicit hierarchy:
  # drill_down:
  #   columns: [year, month, day]        # Ordered coarsest → finest (min 2)
  #   default: month                     # Initial level (optional, defaults to finest)
  #   projections:                        # Optional. Per-level projection overrides
  #     month: roi_monthly               # Projection key for month-level aggregation
  #     year: roi_yearly                 # Projection key for year-level aggregation
  y_inverse: false                      # Optional. Flip Y-axis (0 at top)
  legend_position: bottom               # Optional. bottom | left | right
  reference_lines: []                   # Optional. Horizontal/vertical marker lines
  series: []                            # Optional. Series configuration
  tracks: []                            # Optional. Multi-track panels
  echarts_options: {}                   # Optional. Raw ECharts overrides / full config
```

## Presets

Presets provide pre-configured layouts for common chart patterns:

| Preset | Best for | Default behavior |
|--------|----------|------------------|
| `trend` | Time series | Line chart, date x-axis, auto-detects time column |
| `comparison` | Year-over-year | Groups by year/period, overlays for comparison |
| `breakdown` | Category splits | Stacked bars or grouped bars by category |
| `loss_analysis` | Profit/loss | Horizontal bar, negative values go left |
| `cohort` | Cohort curves | Multi-line, one per cohort group |
| `multi_track` | Stacked panels | Each series → separate panel, shared X-axis |

### Trend chart

```yaml
- id: crm-revenue
  type: chart
  datasource: crm_activity_revenue
  preset: trend
  title: "CRM Activity Revenue"
  series:
    - metric: revenue_net
      type: line
    - metric: all_revenue
      type: line
      label: "Total"
      color: neutral
```

### Comparison chart (YoY)

```yaml
- id: revenue-yoy
  type: chart
  datasource: revenue_metrics_yoy
  preset: comparison
  drill_down:
    columns: [year, month, day]
    default: month
    projections:                          # For ratio metrics only
      month: roi_monthly                  # Re-derives ratio at month level
      year: roi_yearly                    # Re-derives ratio at year level
  title: "Revenue metrics YoY"
  series:
    - metric: costs
      type: bar
      y_axis: left
    - metric: annual_revenue
      type: line
      color: warning
      y_axis: right
```

### Loss analysis

```yaml
- id: revenue-losses
  type: chart
  datasource: revenue_losses_by_language
  preset: loss_analysis
  title: "Revenue Losses by Language"
  series:
    - metric: profit
```

### Cohort chart

```yaml
- id: cohort-cumulative
  type: chart
  datasource: cohort_grow
  preset: cohort
  title: "Cohort grow by days"
  series:
    - metric: cumulative_revenue
      type: line
```

## Sorting

Control X-axis category order. Default: `category_asc` (alphabetical/numeric).

| Value | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `value_desc` | Sort by metric value, largest first |
| `value_asc` | Sort by metric value, smallest first |
| `category_asc` | Sort by category name ascending (default) |
| `category_desc` | Sort by category name descending |
| `none` | Preserve data source order (no sort) |

```yaml
- id: revenue-by-plan
  type: chart
  chart_type: bar
  sort: value_desc
  datasource: revenue_by_plan
  title: "Revenue by Plan Duration"
```

For grouped charts, `value_desc`/`value_asc` sorts by the sum across all groups per category.

## Chart types

Override or specify chart type explicitly:

| Type | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `line` | Line chart |
| `bar` | Bar chart (vertical) |
| `combo` | Mixed bar + line on same axes |

```yaml
- id: bar-chart
  type: chart
  datasource: web5_costs
  chart_type: bar
  title: "Web5 costs"
```

## Series configuration

Each series maps a data column to a visual element:

```yaml
series:
  - metric: costs                       # Required. Column name from data source
    type: line                          # Optional. line | bar | scatter (default: line)
    label: "Costs"                      # Optional. Legend label
    color: warning                      # Optional. Color name or hex
    y_axis: left                        # Optional. left | right (for dual-axis)
    line_width: 3                       # Optional. Line thickness in px (default: 2)
    color_by_value:                     # Optional. Color bars by value sign
      positive: success                 # Color for value >= 0
      negative: destructive             # Color for value < 0
    band:                               # Optional. Confidence interval band
      lower: ci_lower                   # Column with lower bound values
      upper: ci_upper                   # Column with upper bound values
      label: "CI band"                  # Optional. Legend label for the band
    symbol: circle                      # Optional. Marker symbol (scatter)
    symbol_size: 8                      # Optional. Fixed marker size (scatter)
    symbol_size:                        # OR dynamic size from data column
      column: weight                    # Numeric column driving marker size
      min: 6                            # Min marker size in px
      max: 20                           # Max marker size in px
```

### Color values

Use design-system color names or hex values:

- Named colors: `primary`, `secondary`, `warning`, `neutral`, `destructive`, `success`, `danger`
- Hex: `"#3b82f6"`
- Prefer palette-backed colors for multi-series charts; use raw hex only when a named token or canonical palette is not enough.

### `color_by_value`

Conditional bar coloring by value sign. Works in both standard and multi-track charts:

```yaml
series:
  - metric: profit
    type: bar
    color_by_value:
      positive: success                 # green for positive values
      negative: destructive             # red for negative values
```

## Inverted Y-axis

Flip the Y-axis so 0 is at the top and values decrease downward:

```yaml
- id: experiment-dau
  type: chart
  datasource: experiment_data
  y_inverse: true
  title: "DAU uplift"
```

Also available per-track in multi-track charts via `y_inverse: true` on the track.

## Chart title (ECharts canvas)

The `title` property sets the widget header (React component). To also show a title **inside** the ECharts canvas area, use `chart_title`:

```yaml
- id: experiment-dau
  type: chart
  datasource: experiment_data
  title: "Experiment Data"              # Widget header
  chart_title: "Chat started days DAU"  # Inside chart canvas
```

If `chart_title` is omitted, no title renders inside the chart. The two titles are independent.

## Legend position

Control where the legend appears:

```yaml
- id: experiment-dau
  type: chart
  datasource: experiment_data
  legend_position: left                 # bottom (default) | left | right
```

`left` / `right` renders a vertical legend with increased grid margin.

## Reference lines

Add horizontal or vertical reference lines (markLines) to any chart:

```yaml
- id: experiment-chart
  type: chart
  datasource: experiment_data
  reference_lines:
    - axis: y                           # Horizontal line
      value: 0
      label: "Zero"
      color: "#00E5FF"
      style: solid                      # solid | dashed | dotted
    - axis: x                           # Vertical line
      value: "22 Jan"
      label: "Experiment start"
      label_position: bottom              # top | center | bottom (default: top for x, bottom for y)
      color: "#9CA3AF"
      style: dashed
```

## Confidence interval band

Render a shaded area between lower and upper bound columns around a line series:

```yaml
series:
  - metric: test
    type: line
    color: "#FF00FF"
    band:
      lower: ci_lower                   # Column with lower bound
      upper: ci_upper                   # Column with upper bound
      label: "test – uplift CI"         # Legend label for band
```

The band is rendered as a semi-transparent area behind the line.

## Scatter series

Scatter markers for annotations, flags, or discrete data points:

```yaml
series:
  - metric: srm_flag
    type: scatter
    label: "SRM markers"
    symbol: circle                      # circle | diamond | emptyCircle | ...
    symbol_size: 10                     # Fixed size in px
    color: "#C084FC"
```

### Dynamic marker size

Size markers based on a data column value:

```yaml
series:
  - metric: srm_flag
    type: scatter
    label: "SRM markers"
    symbol_size:
      column: srm_weight               # Numeric column driving size
      min: 8                            # Smallest marker (px)
      max: 16                           # Largest marker (px)
    color: "#C084FC"
```

Values are linearly interpolated from the column's data range to `[min, max]` pixel range.

## Multi-track charts

Multiple vertically stacked chart panels sharing the same X-axis. Each panel ("track") has its own Y-axis, title, and series. Hover/crosshair is synchronized across all tracks.

### Explicit tracks (full control)

```yaml
- id: margin-spend
  type: chart
  col_span: 12
  row_span: 2
  datasource: margin_spend_data
  title: "Margin and spend by day"
  tracks:
    - title: "Total margin"             # Y-axis label
      height_ratio: 1                   # Relative height (default 1)
      series:
        - metric: margin
          type: bar
          color_by_value:
            positive: success
            negative: destructive
    - title: "Marketing Costs"
      height_ratio: 1
      series:
        - metric: marketing_costs
          type: line
          color: primary
```

### `preset: multi_track` (shorthand)

Each `series` element auto-becomes a separate track. `label` becomes track title:

```yaml
- id: margin-spend-easy
  type: chart
  col_span: 12
  row_span: 2
  datasource: margin_spend_data
  preset: multi_track
  title: "Margin and spend by day"
  series:
    - metric: margin
      type: bar
      label: "Total margin"
      color_by_value:
        positive: success
        negative: destructive
    - metric: marketing_costs
      type: line
      label: "Marketing Costs"
      color: primary
```

### Track configuration

```yaml
tracks:
  - title: string                       # Optional. Y-axis label for this panel
    height_ratio: number                # Optional. Relative height (default 1)
    y_inverse: boolean                  # Optional. Invert Y-axis for this track
    soft_min: boolean                   # Optional. Soft-clamp Y minimum to 0
    split_area: boolean                 # Optional. Alternating horizontal bands
    area_fill: boolean                  # Optional. Fill area under line series
    zero_line: boolean                  # Optional. Show a dashed zero reference line
    label_every: number                 # Optional. Show value labels every N points
    background_fill: string             # Optional. Track background color (hex)
    borders:                            # Optional. Track border lines
      enabled: boolean
      top: boolean
      bottom: boolean
      left: boolean
      right: boolean
    axis_line:                          # Optional. Y-axis line style
      show: boolean
      color: string
      width: number
      type: solid | dashed | dotted
    series:                             # Required. Series in this panel
      - metric: string
        type: line | bar | scatter
        color: string
        line_width: number
        color_by_value: { positive, negative }
        band: { lower, upper, label }
        symbol_size: number | { column, min, max }
```

## Horizontal layout

Charts work well in horizontal section layout for side-by-side display:

```yaml
sections:
  - id: side-by-side
    title: Side by Side Charts
    layout: horizontal
    columns: 2
    widgets:
      - id: chart-left
        type: chart
        datasource: source_a
        preset: loss_analysis
        series:
          - metric: profit
      - id: chart-right
        type: chart
        datasource: source_b
        preset: trend
        series:
          - metric: revenue_net
            type: line
```

## Full experiment chart example

Combines reference lines, CI band, scatter markers with dynamic size, legend position, and line width:

```yaml
- id: experiment-dau
  type: chart
  col_span: 12
  datasource: experiment_data
  title: "Experiment Data"
  chart_title: "Chat started days DAU"
  legend_position: left
  reference_lines:
    - axis: y
      value: 0
      color: "#00E5FF"
      style: solid
    - axis: x
      value: "22 Jan"
      label: "Experiment start"
      label_position: bottom
      color: "#9CA3AF"
      style: dashed
  series:
    - metric: test
      type: line
      label: "test"
      color: "#FF00FF"
      line_width: 3
      band:
        lower: ci_lower
        upper: ci_upper
        label: "test – uplift CI"
    - metric: control
      type: line
      label: "control"
      color: "#00E5FF"
      line_width: 2
    - metric: srm_flag
      type: scatter
      label: "SRM markers"
      symbol: circle
      symbol_size:
        column: srm_weight
        min: 8
        max: 18
      color: "#C084FC"
```

## Raw ECharts options

Use `echarts_options` to pass arbitrary ECharts configuration. Two modes:

### Raw-only mode

When `echarts_options` is set **without** `series`, `tracks`, or `preset`, the adapter is bypassed entirely and the interpolated object is passed to ECharts as-is.

```yaml
- id: custom-radar
  type: chart
  datasource: radar_data
  echarts_options:
    radar:
      indicator:
        - { name: "Speed", max: 100 }
        - { name: "Power", max: 100 }
    series:
      - type: radar
        data:
          - value: "$column:scores"
```

### Override mode

When `echarts_options` is combined with normal config (`series`, `preset`, `tracks`), the adapter builds the chart normally and then deep-merges `echarts_options` on top. Use this to tweak grid, tooltip, or other options without rewriting the whole chart.

```yaml
- id: tweaked-chart
  type: chart
  datasource: sales_data
  series:
    - metric: revenue
  echarts_options:
    grid:
      left: 120
    tooltip:
      trigger: item
```

### Data interpolation markers

Markers inside `echarts_options` string values are replaced with actual datasource data:

| Marker | Resolves to | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `$column:name` | Array of all values from column `name` | `["20 Jan", "21 Jan"]` |
| `$value:name:agg` | Single aggregated value (`first`, `last`, `min`, `max`, `sum`, `avg`) | `42.5` |
| `$rows` | Full row array (for `dataset.source`) | `[{date:"20 Jan", val:1}]` |

Interpolation also works in `reference_lines` values:

```yaml
reference_lines:
  - axis: x
    value: "$value:experiment_start_date:first"
    label: "Experiment start"
```

### Caveats

- `datasource` is still required — it provides the data for interpolation
- Raw mode bypasses all adapter formatting (axis detection, color palette, formatters, presets)
- Override mode deep-merges: objects are merged recursively, arrays are replaced

## Series format

Explicitly set the number format for a series, overriding the auto-detection based on column names:

```yaml
series:
  - metric: conversion_rate
    format: percent                    # currency | percent | number
  - metric: revenue
    format: currency
  - metric: dau
    format: number
```

Format priority: `series[].format` > `tooltip.format_overrides` > `tooltip.value_format` > auto-detection from column name.

## Data interpolation in titles and labels

Use `$value:col:agg` and `$column:col` markers in `chart_title`, `series[].label`, and `tracks[].title`:

```yaml
- id: revenue-trend
  type: chart
  datasource: daily_revenue
  preset: trend
  chart_title: "Revenue — total $value:revenue:sum|round:0|currency"
  series:
    - metric: revenue
      label: "Revenue ($value:revenue:last|round:0|currency)"
```

Available aggregations: `first`, `last`, `min`, `max`, `sum`, `avg`.

Chained pipes after aggregation: `$value:col:agg|pipe1|pipe2`. Same pipes as tooltip/legend templates: `round:N`, `floor`, `ceil`, `abs`, `sign`, `fixed:N`, `currency`, `percent`, `number`.

## Tooltip configuration

### Simple mode (declarative)

```yaml
tooltip:
  show_percent: true                   # Show % of total per series
  show_change: true                    # Show delta vs previous data point
  show_total: true                     # Show total row at bottom
  value_format: currency               # Override format for all series
  format_overrides:                    # Override format per metric
    revenue: currency
    rate: percent
```

### Template mode (advanced)

```yaml
tooltip:
  template: |
    <b>{x}</b>
    {#series}
    {marker} {name}: <b>{value|round:0|currency}</b> ({percent|round:1}%)
    {/series}
    <hr/>
    Total: <b>{total|round:0|currency}</b>
```

Template tokens:

| Token | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `{x}` | X-axis value |
| `{#series}...{/series}` | Loop over series at current point |
| `{marker}` | ECharts colored dot |
| `{name}` | Series display name |
| `{value}` or `{value\|pipe}` | Series value, optionally piped |
| `{percent}` | Percentage of total |
| `{change}` or `{change\|pipe}` | Delta from previous point |
| `{change_pct}` | Delta as percentage |
| `{total}` or `{total\|pipe}` | Sum of all series |

Pipes can be chained: `{value|round:0|currency}`, `{change|abs|sign}`.

Available pipes:

| Pipe | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `round:N` | Round to N decimal places |
| `floor` | Round down |
| `ceil` | Round up |
| `abs` | Absolute value |
| `sign` | Prefix +/− sign |
| `fixed:N` | Exact N decimal places (string output) |
| `currency` | Format as currency ($1.2K, $3M) |
| `percent` | Format as percent (×100, append %) |
| `number` | Format as abbreviated number (1.2K, 3M) |

When `template` is set, simple options are ignored.

## Legend template

Display aggregated values next to series names in the legend:

```yaml
legend:
  template: "{name}: {last|currency}"
```

Available tokens: `{name}`, `{first}`, `{last}`, `{min}`, `{max}`, `{sum}`, `{avg}`. Pipes can be chained: `{sum|round:0|currency}`, `{avg|round:1}`. Same pipe set as tooltip templates.

## Rules

- `datasource` accepts a string key (from `datasources` or a projection name) OR an inline `{ sql }` object (auto-registered as `type: view`)
- When using `preset`, the chart auto-configures axes, legends, and tooltips
- `drill_down` enables aggregation toggling:
  - `drill_down: true` — auto-detects year/month/day hierarchy (legacy shorthand, renders Day/Month toggle)
  - `drill_down: { columns: [...], default: ... }` — explicit hierarchy with arbitrary levels
  - `columns` ordered from coarsest to finest (min 2). Active level determines `GROUP BY` = `columns.slice(0, indexOf(level) + 1)`
  - `default` is the initial aggregation level (defaults to finest if omitted)
  - `projections` maps drill levels to projection keys. Use for ratio metrics (CPA, ROI) that cannot be summed. The projection re-derives ratios from additive components at each level.
  - Supports non-temporal hierarchies: `{ columns: [region, city] }`
- `tracks` is incompatible with `drill_down` (tracks takes priority)
- `chart_type` overrides the default type from the preset
- If no `series` is provided, the chart auto-detects numeric columns
- `tracks` takes priority over `series` if both are specified
- Multi-track height: use `row_span: 2` or higher for multi-track charts (300px per track, min 400px total)
- `title` is the widget header; `chart_title` is rendered inside the ECharts canvas
- `band` columns (`lower`, `upper`) and `symbol_size.column` are excluded from auto-detected metrics
- Scatter series with dynamic `symbol_size` show the weight column value (with %) in tooltips
- `echarts_options` in raw-only mode bypasses all adapter logic; in override mode it deep-merges on top
